BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:60b1144a2161c681c5e19a82@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260828T215731Z
SUMMARY:I LOVE BOOSTERS (2026)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Browning Cinema New at the Browning Directed by Boots Riley Wit
 h Keke Palmer\, LaKeith Stanfield\, Demi Moore Rated R\, 113 minutes\, DC
 P In English and Mandarin with English subtitles The latest film written 
 and directed by Boots Riley\, one of the most singular and creative brain
 s in the business\, explodes with such abundant color and trenchant comme
 ntary with such innovation that it feels like Jacques Tati is back on the
  playground\, leading us all to a good time while at school. The plot fol
 lows a crew of professional shoplifters led by Corvette (Keke Palmer) who
  take aim at an ultracutthroat and ultrarich and ultrapowerful fashion ma
 ven. The boosting is basically a community service\, and its warmth and h
 ilarity has enough energy to power a movement.\n\nMore Info: https://www.
 visitsouthbend.com/events/i-love-boosters-2026-2/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/i-love-boosters-2026-2/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260828T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260828T223000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:619c4ef84e06b9e2058b7780@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260828T215731Z
SUMMARY:JOSH ROUSE WSG THE SANCHEZ AGENCY TRIO
LOCATION:Stockroom East | 625 E Jefferson Blvd | South Bend\, IN 46617
DESCRIPTION:With brill building wit and a Midwestern sense of melancholy\, 
 Josh Rouse has built a career that spans over 25 years\, reaching back to
  his acclaimed 1998 debut Dressed Up Like Nebraska & continuing to his br
 eakthrough albums 1972 & Nashville. His well-crafted and hook-laden track
 s are coupled with closely-detailed\, well-observed vignettes in his lyri
 cs. Now passing 50\, Josh faces the next phase of his life. “I remember
  seeing Tom Waits on the cover of a magazine with the headline TOM WAITS 
 AT 50.” Josh recalls “ I was in my twenties and that seemed so far of
 f… but he made a great record (Mule Variations) and I hope I have\, too
 .”\n\nAs Rouse drifts into middle age\, his worldview has expanded – 
 family\, travel… life\, which adds even more depth to the songs. Paste 
 Magazine has lauded Rouse\, saying\, “His knack for setting a simple fe
 eling to a breezy melody shines through again and again\,” and this is 
 once again true with his latest album Going Places. So we see the laconic
  “She’s in L.A.\,” the crisp and snappy “The Lonely Postman\,” 
 drenched in almost-Buddy Holly-esque melodies\, and album closer “Stick
  Around” punctuated by its punching horn touches\, a nod to his return 
 to Tennessee and the city’s country-soul history.\n\nMore Info: https:/
 /www.visitsouthbend.com/events/josh-rouse-wsg-the-sanchez-agency-trio/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/josh-rouse-wsg-the-sanchez-agency
 -trio/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260829T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260829T223000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
