BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a7d606ff56133a85d8edfa8b@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260828T215731Z
SUMMARY:THE CHRISTOPHERS (2025)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Select a DateBrowning Cinema New at the Browning Directed by St
 even Soderbergh With Ian McKellen\, Michaela Coel\, James Corden Rated R\
 , 100 minutes\, DCP Steven Soderbergh and Ian McKellen\, two guys with zi
 llions of credits to their filmographies\, team up with the brilliant but
  lesser seen Miachaela Coel (I May Destroy You\, Chewing Gum) in this liv
 ely black comedy. A mainstay of the London art scene since his starry bre
 akout in the creative explosion of the 1960's\, Julian Sklar (McKellen) h
 as drifted into a cluttered\, self-imposed seclusion. His two estranged c
 hildren (James Corden\, Jessica Gunning) enlist Lori (Coel) \, a young pa
 inter and sometime-forger\, to pose as a prospective assistant and gain a
 ccess to a fabled series of unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in
  his home studio\, in a deceptive bid to secure an inheritance for themse
 lves.\n\nMore Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/the-christopher
 s-2025-2/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/the-christophers-2025-2/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260828T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260828T203000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e812f250278f472b57e71493@visitsouthbend.com
DTSTAMP:20260828T215731Z
SUMMARY:THE CHRISTOPHERS (2025)
LOCATION:DeBartolo Performing Arts Center\, 100 Performing Arts Center | No
 tre Dame\, 46556
DESCRIPTION:Browning Cinema New at the Browning Directed by Steven Soderber
 gh With Ian McKellen\, Michaela Coel\, James Corden Rated R\, 100 minutes
 \, DCP Steven Soderbergh and Ian McKellen\, two guys with zillions of cre
 dits to their filmographies\, team up with the brilliant but lesser seen 
 Miachaela Coel (I May Destroy You\, Chewing Gum) in this lively black com
 edy. A mainstay of the London art scene since his starry breakout in the 
 creative explosion of the 1960's\, Julian Sklar (McKellen) has drifted in
 to a cluttered\, self-imposed seclusion. His two estranged children (Jame
 s Corden\, Jessica Gunning) enlist Lori (Coel) \, a young painter and som
 etime-forger\, to pose as a prospective assistant and gain access to a fa
 bled series of unfinished canvases Julian has buried deep in his home stu
 dio\, in a deceptive bid to secure an inheritance for themselves.\n\nMore
  Info: https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/the-christophers-2025-3/
URL:https://www.visitsouthbend.com/events/the-christophers-2025-3/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260829T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260829T230000
